ce_policies\":{\"sensor_update\":{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-05-05T12:52:23.121596885Z\",\"settings_hash\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"policy_type\":\"sensor-update\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-05-05T12:51:37.544605747Z\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"},\"remote_response\":{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-02-10T07:57:59.064362539Z\",\"settings_hash\":\"XXXXXXXX\",\"policy_type\":\"remote-response\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-02-10T07:57:50.610924385Z\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"},\"device_control\":{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-03-25T15:01:28.51681072Z\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-03-25T15:00:22.442519168Z\",\"policy_type\":\"device-control\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"},\"prevention\":{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-04-04T06:54:06.909774295Z\",\"settings_hash\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"policy_type\":\"prevention\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-04-04T06:53:57.135897343Z\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"},\"global_config\":{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-02-10T07:57:53.70275875Z\",\"settings_hash\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"policy_type\":\"globalconfig\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-02-10T07:57:50.610917888Z\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"}},\"cid\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXx\",\"agent_local_time\":\"2019-05-05T15:52:08.172Z\",\"slow_changing_modified_timestamp\":\"2019-05-12T12:37:35Z\",\"service_pack_major\":\"0\",\"device_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"system_product_name\":\"Latitude XXXX\",\"product_type\":\"1\",\"local_ip\":\"1.1.1.1\",\"external_ip\":\"1.1.1.1\",\"major_version\":\"10\",\"platform_id\":\"0\",\"config_id_base\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"policies\":[{\"applied\":true,\"applied_date\":\"2019-04-04T06:54:06.909774295Z\",\"settings_hash\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\",\"policy_type\":\"prevention\",\"assigned_date\":\"2019-04-04T06:53:57.135897343Z\",\"policy_id\":\"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"}],\"agent_version\":\"4.26.XXXX.0\",\"pointer_size\":\"8\",\"last_seen\":\"2019-05-13T07:21:30Z\"}]","DisplayResult":true}],"Parameters":[{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"","DisplayName":"Customer ID","Description":"Specify the ID of the customer for which you want to execute the action.","OptionalValues":[]},{"Type":"List","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"Equal","DisplayName":"Filter Logic","Description":"Specify what logic should be used, when searching for hosts.","OptionalValues":["Equal","Contains"]},{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"","DisplayName":"Filter Value","Description":"Specify the value that should be used to filter hosts.","OptionalValues":[]},{"Type":"String","ActionId":0,"Id":0,"Mandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"50","DisplayName":"Max Hosts To Return","Description":"Specify how many hosts to return. Default: 50. Maximum: 1000.","OptionalValues":[]}],"AICategories":[],"AIDescription":"### General Description\nThe **List Hosts** action retrieves a list of devices (hosts) from the CrowdStrike Falcon platform based on specified filtering criteria. This action is primarily used for asset discovery, identifying systems with specific attributes (like OS or status), or finding devices associated with particular network identifiers. It provides detailed metadata for each matching host, including OS version, last seen timestamp, and containment status.\n\n### Parameters Description\n| Parameter | Type | Mandatory | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Hostname | String | No | Filter by the name of the machine. Supports prefix and suffix searching with wildcards (e.g., `abc*` or `*abc`). |\n| Local IP | String | No | Filter by the device's local IP address. |\n| External IP | String | No | Filter by the device's external IP address as seen by CrowdStrike. |\n| MAC Address | String | No | Filter by the hardware MAC address of the device. |\n| Platform | String | No | Filter by the operating system platform (e.g., Windows, Mac, Linux). |\n| Status | String | No | Filter by the containment status of the machine (e.g., normal, contained). |\n| Limit | Integer | No | The maximum number of hosts to return in the results. |\n| Include Hidden Hosts | Boolean | No | If set to true, the search will include hosts that have been hidden in the Falcon console. |\n\n### Flow Description\n1. **Authentication**: The action authenticates with the CrowdStrike API using the provided Client ID and Secret to obtain a bearer token.\n2. **Query Construction**: It builds a Falcon Query Language (FQL) filter string based on the provided input parameters (Hostname, IP, MAC, etc.).\n3. **Search**: It calls the `/devices/queries/devices/v1` endpoint (and optionally `/devices/queries/devices-hidden/v1`) to retrieve a list of matching device IDs.\n4. **Detail Retrieval**: For the retrieved IDs, it performs a secondary call to the `/devices/entities/devices/v2` endpoint to fetch comprehensive metadata for each host.\n5. **Output**: The action returns the list of device objects and populates a results table in the Google SecOps interface.\n\n### Additional Notes\nIf no filters are provided, the action will return a list of all hosts up to the specified limit. This action is read-only and does not modify any data in CrowdStrike or Google SecOps.","EntityTypes":["ADDRESS","HOSTNAME"]}